# ABI i386 tls: thread-local storage (NOT a psABI group)
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The i386 psABI only names the relocation types for thread-local storage and
# refers to a separate TLS document that was not in the source set used to
# write this suite. These assertions are therefore outside the psABI oracle:
# the oracle is the C language's thread storage duration (every thread has its
# own object, initialised from the initial value or zero, with the alignment
# asked for), which the TLS layout (.tdata and .tbss) implements. They are kept
# in an area of their own so that the ids show it: ABI.i386.tls.NNN.

assertion  ABI.i386.tls.001
anchor     i386-psabi:object-files#Relocation types for thread-local storage (R_386_TLS_*), which refer to the separate ELF TLS document (not in the source set)
class      required
says       A thread-local object with an initialiser (the .tdata image) starts in every
           new thread with that initial value, whatever other threads have written to
           their own copies.
note       Not a psABI group: the oracle is the C language's thread storage duration,
           which the TLS layout implements; the TLS document the psABI refers to was
           not in the source set.
test       t/001-tls-initialised.c
nomutant   the behaviour belongs to the thread library and the system; the detectors are validated by abi/control.sh

assertion  ABI.i386.tls.002
anchor     i386-psabi:object-files#Relocation types for thread-local storage (R_386_TLS_*), which refer to the separate ELF TLS document (not in the source set)
class      required
says       A thread-local object without an initialiser (the .tbss part, here a
           20000-byte array, a word and a structure) is all zero in every new thread,
           even when another thread has filled its own copy.
note       Not a psABI group: the oracle is the C language's thread storage duration,
           which the TLS layout implements; the TLS document the psABI refers to was
           not in the source set.
test       t/002-tls-zero.c
nomutant   the behaviour belongs to the thread library and the system; the detectors are validated by abi/control.sh

assertion  ABI.i386.tls.003
anchor     i386-psabi:object-files#Relocation types for thread-local storage (R_386_TLS_*), which refer to the separate ELF TLS document (not in the source set)
class      required
says       Four threads alive at the same time, and the main thread, each have their
           own copy of an initialised and of an uninitialised thread-local variable:
           the addresses differ and each thread reads back the value it wrote.
note       Not a psABI group: the oracle is the C language's thread storage duration,
           which the TLS layout implements; the TLS document the psABI refers to was
           not in the source set.
test       t/003-tls-distinct.c
nomutant   the behaviour belongs to the thread library and the system; the detectors are validated by abi/control.sh

assertion  ABI.i386.tls.004
anchor     i386-psabi:object-files#Relocation types for thread-local storage (R_386_TLS_*), which refer to the separate ELF TLS document (not in the source set)
class      required
says       Thread-local objects declared with an alignment of 16, 64, 256 and 4096
           bytes (both with an initialiser and without) are aligned that way in every
           thread.
note       Not a psABI group: the oracle is the C language's thread storage duration,
           which the TLS layout implements; the TLS document the psABI refers to was
           not in the source set.
test       t/004-tls-alignment.c
nomutant   the behaviour belongs to the thread library and the system; the detectors are validated by abi/control.sh

